[00:11.11]We’re still in Ireland.
[00:13.06]We arrived in Dublin four days ago.
[00:16.00]My sister and I liked it a lot – it was great – we weren’t bored at all!
[00:21.38]Then yesterday, after lunch, Dad hired a car and we travelled to the west of Ireland – it didn’t take very long, just about two and a half hours, but that was a bit boring.
[00:34.58]But, after two hours, Dad turned round to us and said: ‘We’ve got a surprise for you.
[00:40.64]Tonight our hotel is a castle! How exciting is that!’
[00:45.36]A joke, right? Wrong!
[00:47.96]We didn’t think he was serious, but he was!
[00:50.22]At the end of the journey, we stopped outside a real castle.
[00:56.16]A nice lady welcomed us and started to show us around.
[01:00.30]What an amazing place!
[01:02.58]Can you believe that we walked up fifty stone steps to get to the living room?
[01:07.66]The castle is over 600 years old, but it had everything we needed.
[01:13.36]There was a bedroom for our parents and we each had a bedroom, too.
[01:17.78]But I didn’t sleep very well last night – I was so excited to be in a real castle!
[01:24.28]This morning we had breakfast and then we climbed up to the top of the castle.
[01:29.28]We were amazed at the beautiful countryside around us.
[01:33.42]Then it started to rain and there was a fantastic rainbow – I love rainbows!
[01:38.88]The place was so great, we didn’t want to leave.
[01:42.74]This afternoon we want to go to Limerick, so we’re packing our bags again!
[01:47.76]Can it be as good as a castle? Let’s see.
